{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787588103,"nonce":"5z7CoPv+V0Dl65xZXWfwIbyvN+w=","message":"CLOSED 2026-08-24: premise reversed. ADR-0063 was amended (2026-08-23 pointer, CONTEXT.md updated): Step log bytes are authoritative in the OBJECT STORE; the Depot may cache chunks for a fast live tail but its copy is never authoritative — the opposite of this slice's \"move logs onto the Depot\". The motivating defect is also structurally fixed by ADR-0067 (PR #95): the LocalDir-on-emptyDir silent fallback no longer exists (no silent object-store default, boot fails closed without a reachable store), so logs can no longer silently die on a Pod roll. The still-good ideas here — the three-branch read path with absence authoritative, and the volume-identity marker — were partially absorbed by ADR-0063 part 5/6 as amended; anything left should be re-ticketed against the object-store log path, not this one.","files":null}]}